WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.940
- So Alex Jones is defaulted, again.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.350
It's like Groundhog Day over here.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.910
This time in Connecticut,

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.400
where he faces additional defamation suits

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.430
that like the court case in
Texas, he has defaulted on

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.650
because of all the
shenanigans in discovery.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.960
This time it's over some Google Analytics.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.640
Basically, the judge
kept telling Alex Jones

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.320
and his companies to
turn over data related

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.350
to Google Analytics and
they refused to do so,

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.600
and that data definitely existed,

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.550
which the plaintiffs found out about

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:27.750
and brought it to the judge.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.333
- This stunningly cavalier
attitude with respect

00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:36.333
to their discovery obligations
is what led to the default

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.190
in the first place.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:41.310
- And as a sanction, Jones
cannot argue that he did not

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.680
make a profit from the
Sandy Hook Coverage.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.732
- Court Hereby sanctions the
defendants by precluding them

00:00:47.732 --> 00:00:50.550
from presenting evidence or argument

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.120
that they did not profit
from the Sandy Hook coverage.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.500
- So basically, the Connecticut cases

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.593
are going just as poorly for
Jones as the Texas case did.

